`gazzali/cohort/vendor/core/` and `gazzali/cohort/vendor/biostats/` are copied from
**CohortStudio** by Karim El Mernissi, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see `LICENSE` in this directory).

- Upstream: https://github.com/KarimELMERNISSI/Cohort-Studio
- Version: 2.4.1
- DOI: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23436094

## What was taken

| Vendored | Why |
|---|---|
| `core/criteria.py`, `core/population.py` | Criterion families, row-preserving filtering, population fingerprint |
| `core/attrition.py` | The participant-flow model (STROBE item 13) and its consistency check |
| `core/fingerprint.py`, `core/lineage.py` | Content fingerprints, row identity, the SHA-256 hash chain |
| `core/expressions/` | The whitelisted expression sandbox used by derived variables and criteria |
| `biostats/` (whole package) | Welch-first comparisons, effect sizes with confidence intervals, post-hoc tests, multiplicity corrections, normality and MCAR diagnostics, and the multiple-imputation engine with Rubin's-rules pooling |

## What was deliberately not taken

The upstream Streamlit application (`app_pages/`, `ui/`), its storage layer (DuckDB and
per-user workspaces), its identity provider (`manage/iam/`), the retrieval/graph
features (`manage/rag*`, `graph/`), its configuration schema (`CMP_*`) and the
proprietary yFiles renderer.

## Local modifications

Two changes, and no others.

**1. Imports.** Absolute imports were rewritten so the packages live under this
namespace:

```
from core.<module>      ->  from gazzali.cohort.vendor.core.<module>
from biostats.<module>  ->  from gazzali.cohort.vendor.biostats.<module>
```

**2. One syntax fix, upstream bug.** `biostats/mi/analyze.py` line 67 reads
`except TypeError, ValueError:` upstream — Python 2 syntax, a `SyntaxError` under
Python 3 that makes the whole `biostats.mi` package unimportable at the pinned
revision (2.4.1). It was corrected to `except (TypeError, ValueError):`. This is the
only semantic edit; report it upstream.

The vendored tree is excluded from `ruff` (see `pyproject.toml`) so that a future
re-sync stays a clean diff. Keep it byte-identical apart from those two rewrites.

## Method citations

`biostats/references.py` carries the citation for each method (Steiger 2004 for the
noncentral-t interval, Barnard & Rubin 1999 for the degrees of freedom, Little 1988
for the MCAR test, Bergsma 2013 for the bias-corrected Cramér's V, and so on). Those
strings surface in analysis results and must be preserved: they are both a licence
condition and an academic-honesty requirement.

## R parity of the imputation engine

Carried over: `tests/pm/fixtures/mi/` (`mice_reference.json`, `mice_completed_long.csv`,
generated by `tests/reference/r/make_mi_fixtures.R` upstream) and
`tests/pm/test_cohort_mi_parity.py`. They check the pooling against R `mice` 3.19 and
`mitml` 0.4.5: 1e-10 for `pool_scalar`, 1e-8 loss of the linear model, 1e-6 logistic,
1e-5 for Poisson and Cox (R's own convergence tolerance is the limit there), and the
D1/D2 tests and pooled R-squared as well.

These fixtures are the reason multiple imputation is allowed in this module at all. Do
not remove them, and re-run them after any change to `biostats/mi/`.
